## mocking void methods using doNothing()

//Arrange
doNothing().when(myRepository).deleteById(id);

//Assert
verify(myService, times(1)).deleteById(id);

=======================================================================================

## difference between when() and doThrow() for void methods

void deleteById(Long id);      //if method return type is void but can still throw exception
                               //prefer doThrow() over when() because when() always expects a return value

when(myRepository.deleteById(id)).thenThrow(new RuntimeException("Invalid user ID"));
doThrow(new RuntimeException("Invalid user ID")).when(myRepository).deleteById(id);

